<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Martin de Porres</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1579–1639</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Saint Martin de Porres</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Martin de Porres was a lay brother of the Dominican order in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a>, the son of a Spanish nobleman and a freed Black woman from Panama. Known for his care for the sick and the poor, he became one of the most popular saints of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin-america">Latin America</a> and was canonised in 1962 as the first Black saint of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>. He is the patron saint of people of mixed race and of social justice.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/martin-de-porres.jpg" alt="Martin de Porres" width="260" height="350" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:San_Martin_de_Porres_huaycan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
